
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Online Exam</title>

    <style>
        body {
            background-color: #b2e5d8;
            font-family: "Times New Roman";
            font-size: 20px;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
        }

        h3 {
            text-align: center;
        }

        .details {
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        }

        .question {
            margin-top: 25px;
        }

        input[type="text"],
        input[type="date"] {
            padding: 5px;
            font-size: 16px;
        }

        .buttons {
            text-align: center;
            margin-top: 30px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <h1>ONLINE EXAM</h1>

    <form>

        <div class="details">

            Enter your name:
            <input type="text" name="name" required>
            <br><br>

            Register No:
            <input type="text" name="regno" required>
            <br><br>

            Date:
            <input type="date" name="date" required>

        </div>

        <h3>QUESTIONS</h3>
        <h4 style="text-align:center;">
            Attend all the questions
        </h4>

        <div class="question">
            1. What does HTML stand for?<br><br>

            <input type="radio" name="q1" value="a" required>
            Hyper Text Markup Language<br>

            <input type="radio" name="q1" value="b">
            High Text Machine Language<br>

            <input type="radio" name="q1" value="c">
            Simple Markup Language
        </div>

        <div class="question">
            2. How many heading tags are available in HTML?<br><br>

            <input type="radio" name="q2" value="a" required>
            6<br>

            <input type="radio" name="q2" value="b">
            4<br>

            <input type="radio" name="q2" value="c">
            3
        </div>

        <div class="question">
            3. What is the difference between opening and closing tags?<br><br>

            <input type="radio" name="q3" value="a" required>
            Both have slash<br>

            <input type="radio" name="q3" value="b">
            Closing tag has a slash<br>

            <input type="radio" name="q3" value="c">
            There is no difference
        </div>

        <div class="question">
            4. Which tag is used to create a hyperlink?<br><br>

            <input type="radio" name="q4" value="a" required>
            &lt;a&gt;<br>

            <input type="radio" name="q4" value="b">
            &lt;p&gt;<br>

            <input type="radio" name="q4" value="c">
            &lt;h1&gt;
        </div>

        <div class="question">
            5. Which tag is used to insert an image?<br><br>

            <input type="radio" name="q5" value="a" required>
            &lt;img&gt;<br>

            <input type="radio" name="q5" value="b">
            &lt;table&gt;<br>

            <input type="radio" name="q5" value="c">
            &lt;body&gt;
        </div>

        <div class="buttons">
            <input type="submit" value="Submit">
            <input type="reset" value="Reset">
        </div>

    </form>

</body>
</html>
